  "id": "ENT096",
  "title": "The Key That Lived in the Other Pocket",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "everyday microdramas",
  "premise": "A commuter wants to leave on time, but searches the same jacket pocket after every distraction. They empty both pockets onto two labeled circles, spot the key under a folded note, and choose a single small tray by the exit for its return that evening.",
  "hook": "I checked that pocket. I checked that pocket again.",
  "visible_action": "Hands revisit one pocket; objects tumble into two circles; note unfolds and exposes key; evening cut shows key landing in a tray.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Make a repeated search visible and give the item a repeatable home.",
  "gate": "A fictional organization choice, not a guarantee about memory or attention.",
